<!-- ═══════════════ SECTION 5: KEY RATIOS ═══════════════ -->

<section class="section" id="sec-ratios">
  <h2>10 Financial Ratios Every Hospital Leader Must Know</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">These ratios, identified by the Flex Monitoring Team and the National Rural Health Resource Center, form the core financial health assessment for Critical Access Hospitals.</p>

  <div class="grid grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header"><div class="icon" style="background:var(--green-bg);color:var(--green);">📊</div> Total Margin</div>
      <div class="formula-box"><span class="sym">(Total Revenue − Total Expenses)</span> <span class="op">÷</span> <span class="sym">Total Revenue</span></div>
      <p>Measures overall profitability including non-operating income (investments, donations). <strong>Benchmark: 2–4%.</strong> A hospital with consistently negative total margin is on a trajectory toward financial distress.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header"><div class="icon" style="background:var(--blue-bg);color:var(--blue);">📊</div> Operating Margin</div>
      <div class="formula-box"><span class="sym">(Operating Revenue − Operating Expenses)</span> <span class="op">÷</span> <span class="sym">Operating Revenue</span></div>
      <p>Measures profitability from core healthcare operations only. <strong>Benchmark: 0–3%.</strong> This is the truest measure of the hospital's business sustainability, as it excludes volatile non-operating items.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header"><div class="icon" style="background:var(--gold-bg);color:var(--gold);">💰</div> Days Cash on Hand</div>
      <div class="formula-box"><span class="sym">(Cash + Short-term Investments)</span> <span class="op">÷</span> <span class="sym">(Operating Expenses − Depreciation) ÷ 365</span></div>
      <p>How many days the hospital could continue to operate using only its available cash. <strong>Benchmark: 60–120 days.</strong> Below 30 days is a crisis indicator — the hospital may not be able to make payroll.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header"><div class="icon" style="background:var(--purple-bg);color:var(--purple);">⚖</div> Current Ratio</div>
      <div class="formula-box"><span class="sym">Current Assets</span> <span class="op">÷</span> <span class="sym">Current Liabilities</span></div>
      <p>Measures ability to pay short-term obligations. <strong>Benchmark: 1.5–2.5.</strong> Below 1.0 means the hospital owes more in the short term than it has available to pay.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header"><div class="icon" style="background:var(--orange-bg);color:var(--orange);">🏗</div> Age of Plant</div>
      <div class="formula-box"><span class="sym">Accumulated Depreciation</span> <span class="op">÷</span> <span class="sym">Annual Depreciation Expense</span></div>
      <p>Indicates how old the facility and equipment are on average. <strong>Benchmark: &lt;12 years.</strong> Many CAHs have age of plant exceeding 15–20 years, indicating deferred capital investment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header"><div class="icon" style="background:var(--red-bg);color:var(--red);">📉</div> Debt Service Coverage</div>
      <div class="formula-box"><span class="sym">(Net Income + Depreciation + Interest)</span> <span class="op">÷</span> <span class="sym">(Principal + Interest Payments)</span></div>
      <p>Ability to repay debt obligations. <strong>Benchmark: &gt;2.0.</strong> Below 1.25 typically triggers loan covenant violations. Below 1.0 means the hospital cannot cover its debt payments from operations.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

